# ProjectAI Frontend Rules

ProjectAI frontend is a Control Center, not a developer-only admin table.

User-facing UI language is Russian.

Do not translate technical identifiers such as:
- SBER
- LKOH
- MOEX
- RUB
- UUID
- model IDs

Backend enums remain technical. Translate them in the presentation layer.

Do not scatter UI labels and enum translations across JSX.
Use centralized presentation mappings/utilities.

Frontend communicates with ProjectAI only through API.

Do not perform heavy analytics in the browser.

API access belongs in the frontend API/data layer, not scattered across components.

Pages must handle:
- loading;
- empty;
- error;
- success.

Prefer readable information hierarchy over dense technical tables.

Technical implementation details may be available in drill-down views but should not dominate normal user screens.

Avoid:
- giant components;
- unnecessary UI frameworks;
- decorative complexity;
- fake data on unfinished product pages.

Placeholder sections must clearly say they are not implemented.

Use reusable components where they remove real duplication, but do not build a large design system prematurely.

Always verify UI changes against real current ProjectAI data, not only mocked tests.
